          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">how you besiege me (and feed me)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;It was natural, right? To want that for herself: someone to tell her who she was, in her entirety, in her truth, whenever she forgot. For her heart to lurch forward and go &lt;i&gt;God, give it to me, where do I start&lt;/i&gt; and then fall flat when it came up empty, like expecting a three-course meal only to end up swallowing air.&lt;br /&gt;Adora had always been good at self-control - one of the perks of a life spent in service of whatever she thought was the greater good. But now this &lt;i&gt;hunger&lt;/i&gt; had started in her, and there was nothing preventing it from developing further.&lt;br /&gt;And it was all Catraâ€™s fault.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A year after the war, Adora returns to Etheria. She finds everything has changed, except the thing that really should have.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>nuttyshake</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
